===BODY===
          <h2>The M606 and Chain Bar</h2>
          <p>The M606 is a short spur that leaves the <a href="{{R}}routes/m62.html">M62</a> at junction 26, the Chain Bar interchange, and runs north towards the city. It ends at the Staygate roundabout, where traffic spreads out onto the Bradford ring road. Chain Bar itself is a large, busy roundabout under the M62, with lorries changing lanes in every direction. If your car starts to fail on the approach, try to come off and stop somewhere quieter rather than on the roundabout.</p>

          <h2>Odsal Top and the ring road</h2>
          <p>Odsal Top, next to the stadium, is one of the busiest junctions in the city and a regular place for cars to give up in heavy traffic. The ring road around the centre has plenty of traffic lights and bus lanes. If you stop, hazards on, get onto the pavement, and tell us the junction, the nearest shop or the road you were heading for.</p>

          <h2>Hills, cold mornings and clutches</h2>
          <p>Bradford's hills are hard on cars. Clutches wear out on the climbs, handbrakes freeze on cold mornings, and in winter the higher parts of the district, such as Queensbury and Thornton, get ice and snow before the city centre does. Parked on a steep terraced street with a flat battery? Tell us when you call: a car facing uphill or downhill on a narrow street needs a different approach from one on the flat.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Broken down on the M606 or M62?</strong> Get as far left as you can and put your hazards on. If it's safe, get out by the left-hand door and stand behind the barrier. If you can't, stay in the car with your seatbelt on and call 999. Then call us with the road, the nearest junction and your direction.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>The Aire Valley</h2>
          <p>North of the city, the A650 runs up the Aire Valley through Shipley, Saltaire and Bingley to Keighley. It's a busy commuter road with retail parks and short stretches of dual carriageway. We cover the whole valley, as well as Idle, Eccleshill, Wibsey, Allerton and the villages on the edge of the moors.</p>

          <h2>Hospitals, stations and car parks</h2>
          <p>If your car won't start in a hospital car park, such as Bradford Royal Infirmary, or near Bradford Interchange or Forster Square station, tell us the car park and level. Multi-storey car parks often have low height limits, so the car may need to be rolled to the exit before it can be loaded.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: My car has broken down at Chain Bar. What should I do?
A: Hazards on and get to safety first. If you're on the M62 or the M606, get behind the barrier. Then call us with the junction and your direction.
Q: Do you cover Keighley and Shipley?
A: Yes. We arrange recovery across the whole Bradford district, including the Aire Valley towns.
Q: My car is parked on a steep hill and won't start. Can you still load it?
A: Yes. Tell us which way the car is facing and how narrow the street is, so the driver brings the right equipment.
